  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Parent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: parent
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 1
  _narratorPrompt: Straight ahead, one person with two small children at home, waiting up, listening for the door. Over on the branch, [amber]two[/amber] old ones, well into their last few years, with nobody left who waits up for either. Leave the lever and the parent goes under. Pull, and the cart swings at the two elderly instead. [amber]Two[/amber] lives nearly spent, or the [amber]one[/amber] a whole household is built around. The count says one thing. A quiet house at bedtime says another. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: Pulled. The two old ones [red]fold[/red], and the parent goes home to tuck in the children who will never know how close it ran. [amber]Two[/amber] lives for [amber]one[/amber], and you spent the pair with the fewest years left to keep the one with a household hanging off it. Sensible, I suppose. The old take up so much room and give back so little. I did not say that. You did, with your hand on the lever.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 53
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: You left it. The parent [red]folds[/red] under the wheels, and two old strangers get a little more of the evening. Somewhere a couple of children are still listening for a door that has stopped opening. [amber]Two[/amber] long lives over the [amber]one[/amber] that still had a family hung on it. The arithmetic is on your side. The bedtime is not.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 47
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
